Extract your internal Google Cloud project parameters dynamically, construct the Artifact Registry repository, 
configure Docker's secure handshake, and dispatch the asset.

Code:

# 1. Set environment variables dynamically
export PROJECT_ID=$(gcloud config get-value project)
export REGION=us-west1
export REPO_NAME=valkyrie-repository

# 2. Create the Artifact Registry repository
gcloud artifacts repositories create $REPO_NAME \
    --repository-format=docker \
    --location=$REGION \
    --description="Valkyrie Docker Repository"

# 3. Authenticate Docker to communicate securely with Artifact Registry
gcloud auth configure-docker $REGION-docker.pkg.dev --quiet

# 4. Re-tag your image matching the required structural schema
docker tag valkyrie-prod:v0.0.3 $REGION-docker.pkg.dev/$PROJECT_ID/$REPO_NAME/valkyrie-prod:v0.0.3

# 5. Push the built image to your repository
docker push $REGION-docker.pkg.dev/$PROJECT_ID/$REPO_NAME/valkyrie-prod:v0.0.3



